  "question": {
    "text": "If&nbsp;<math><mi>P</mi></math> and <math><mi>Q</mi></math> are points with eccentric angles <math><mi>θ</mi></math> and <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>π</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>6</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math> on the ellipse <math><mfrac><mrow><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>16</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mrow><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo></math> then the area (in sq. units) of the triangle <math><mi>O</mi><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi></math> (where <math><mi>O</mi></math> is the origin) is equal to",
    "image": null
